            <div xml:id="d121">

                <pb facs="0217" n="115" xml:id="pg115"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/438–439.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Chargé de
                    Billier.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-12-08"><hi rendition="#italic">December 8,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 34.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The department acknowledges the receipt of
                    your unnumbered dispatch of the 11th ultimo, with which was inclosed a copy of
                    the Persian Government’s acceptance of the invitation of this Government to send
                    delegates to the joint commission on the opium question at Shanghai.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to express anew to the foreign office the gratification of
                    this Government that Persia will participate in a conference which, it is hoped,
                    will be instrumental in contributing toward the suppression of the opium
                    evil.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
